# mdedit CLI — Agent Skill

> Use this skill to manage articles, folders, workspaces, and API keys on [mdedit.ai](https://mdedit.ai) directly from your terminal or from an AI agent.

## Install

```bash
npm install -g mdedit-cli
```

## Quick-start authentication

```bash
# Set your API key (get one at https://docs.mdedit.ai/api-keys)
mdedit config login --api-key <YOUR_KEY>

# Or via environment variable (recommended for CI/agents)
export MDEDIT_API_KEY=<YOUR_KEY>
export MDEDIT_WORKSPACE_ID=<YOUR_WORKSPACE_ID>   # optional default workspace
```

## Agent tips

- **Always use `--format json`** when parsing output programmatically: `mdedit article list --format json`
- **Suppress interactive prompts** by supplying all required flags (title, name, …) on the command line.
- **Use `-y` / `--yes`** on destructive commands to skip confirmation prompts.
- **Pipe article content** via stdin using `--file -` or read it back with `--content-only` (stdout).
- In `json` mode, **human-facing messages go to stderr** (stdout stays machine-parseable).
- **Exit codes**: `0` = success, `1` = error. Errors are written to stderr.

## Global flags

| Flag | Description |
|------|-------------|
| `-F, --format <plain\|table\|json>` | Output format. Use `json` for agents. |
| `--api-key <key>` | Override API key for this call |
| `--workspace <workspaceId>` | Override default workspace for this call |
| `--api-url <url>` | Override API base URL |
| `--local` | Target local API at `http://localhost:8080` |
| `--debug` | Print stack traces and request info on errors |

## Commands reference

### config

```bash
mdedit config show                          # show current config (api key redacted)
mdedit config login --api-key <key>         # authenticate
mdedit config logout                        # remove stored api key
mdedit config use-workspace <workspaceId>   # set default workspace
mdedit config set <key> <value>             # set any config key
mdedit config clear --yes                   # wipe all config
```

### workspace

```bash
mdedit workspace list
mdedit workspace get <workspaceId>
mdedit workspace create --name "My Workspace" --type user
mdedit workspace update <workspaceId> --name "New Name"
mdedit workspace delete <workspaceId> --yes
```

### folder

```bash
mdedit folder list [-w <workspaceId>]
mdedit folder list --include-deleted
mdedit folder get <folderId>
mdedit folder create --name "Drafts" [--parent <parentFolderId>]
mdedit folder update <folderId> --name "Archive"
mdedit folder delete <folderId> --yes
```

### article

```bash
# List & filter
mdedit article list
mdedit article list --folder <folderId>
mdedit article list --limit 10 --offset 0

# Read
mdedit article get <articleId>
mdedit article get <articleId> --content-only        # raw markdown to stdout
mdedit article get <articleId> --include-content     # include markdown in output object
mdedit article get <articleId> --output article.md   # save markdown to file

# Create
mdedit article create --title "My Article"
mdedit article create --title "My Article" --folder <folderId> --file article.md
mdedit article create --title "My Article" --content "# Hello world"
echo "# Hello" | mdedit article create --title "My Article" --file -

# Update
mdedit article update <articleId> --title "New Title"
mdedit article update <articleId> --file updated.md
mdedit article update <articleId> --content "# Updated"
cat updated.md | mdedit article update <articleId> --file -
mdedit article update <articleId> --archive
mdedit article update <articleId> --pin

# Delete
mdedit article delete <articleId> --yes

# Export
mdedit article export <articleId> --output article.zip
```

### api-key

```bash
mdedit apikey list
mdedit apikey create --name "CI/CD Key" --description "Used in pipeline"
mdedit apikey create --name "30-day key" --expires 30
mdedit apikey revoke <keyId> --yes
```

### utility

```bash
mdedit health    # check API health
mdedit info      # CLI version, API URL, workspace, auth status
```

### skill

```bash
mdedit skill show                             # print this skill to stdout
mdedit skill install                          # install skill into all detected agent tools
mdedit skill install --target claude          # Claude Code: ~/.claude/CLAUDE.md
mdedit skill install --target cursor          # Cursor: .cursor/rules/mdedit.mdc
mdedit skill install --target codex           # GitHub Copilot: .github/copilot-instructions.md
mdedit skill install --target all             # all of the above
mdedit skill install --global                 # install globally (home directory targets)
```

## Common agent workflows

### Workflow: read an article and update its content

```bash
# Fetch current content
CONTENT=$(mdedit article get <articleId> --content-only)

# Modify $CONTENT with your agent logic, then push it back
echo "$MODIFIED_CONTENT" | mdedit article update <articleId> --file -
```

### Workflow: create a new article in a folder

```bash
# Find the target folder
mdedit folder list --format json | jq '.[] | select(.name=="Docs") | .id'

# Create article in that folder
mdedit article create --title "API Reference" --folder <folderId> --file api-ref.md
```

### Workflow: bulk export all articles as JSON

```bash
mdedit article list --format json > articles.json
```

### Workflow: set up a fresh environment

```bash
export MDEDIT_API_KEY=<key>
mdedit config login --api-key "$MDEDIT_API_KEY"
# list workspaces and set the default
mdedit workspace list --format json
mdedit config use-workspace <workspaceId>
```

## Environment variables

| Variable | Description |
|----------|-------------|
| `MDEDIT_API_KEY` | API key (overrides stored config) |
| `MDEDIT_API_URL` | API base URL (default: `https://apiv2.mdedit.ai`) |
| `MDEDIT_WORKSPACE_ID` | Default workspace ID |
| `MDEDIT_CONFIG_DIR` | Override config directory (default: `~/.mdedit-cli`) |
| `MDEDIT_DEBUG` | Set to `1` to enable debug output |

## Output format guide

| Format | Best for |
|--------|----------|
| `table` | Humans scanning many rows (default) |
| `plain` | Human reading (object details) |
| `json` | Agents, scripts, piping to `jq` |

Use `--format json` globally: `mdedit <command> --format json`.
In `json` mode all human-readable messages go to **stderr** so stdout stays machine-parseable.

## Error handling

Errors write a descriptive message to **stderr** and exit with code `1`.

Common errors and fixes:

| HTTP | Meaning | Fix |
|------|---------|-----|
| 401 | Unauthenticated | Run `mdedit config login --api-key <key>` |
| 403 | Forbidden | Check API key workspace permissions |
| 404 | Not found | Verify IDs and `--api-url` |

Add `--debug` to print full stack traces.
